Here KLD measures how much information is lost by national signature ci when approximated with the national signature from cj. In other words, the less information that is lost by approximating ci with cj, the more similar cj is to ci. From here, we construct 4,914 international networks of topic similarity across nearly 150 academic fields and 33 years of data (that is, 1980 to 2012), defined as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
